[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Gyro variant: the plain profile plus pointer movement by tilting the controller. Hold Select and Start together to pause the gyro (clutch).
The right stick {rs} moves the pointer: {rt} or {south} is a left click (select a unit, a hex or a target), {lt} a right click. The left stick {ls} pans the camera.
{north} is Space, which confirms a move or attack and ends actions. {east} or {start} is Escape: it cancels, and opens the game menu.
{lb} and {rb} step back and forward through your units (Shift Tab and Tab). The {updown} d-pad zooms and {leftright} rotates the camera (Q and E).
{select} lists the weapon keys 1 to 6 (tap it, pick with {south}). Hold {west} for Shift, hold {l3} for Alt, and click {r3} for the middle mouse button (drag to orbit).
Hold {guide} and press {west} for the on-screen keyboard (naming mechs and pilots).
BattleTech has no controller support. INFERRED, not checked on an install: Space as confirm, Tab and Shift Tab for unit cycling, Q and E rotation, Alt for details, and the number keys for weapons. The game has key remapping in its options; edit these to match.'''

